problems.problem:
The following arithmetic series is given:

$$\mathbf{1 \qquad 5 \qquad 9 \qquad 13 \qquad 17 \qquad 21 \qquad \ldots}$$

where the first term is **1** and the remaining terms are generated by adding **4** to the previous term.

The Pascal program below was created to print on the same line the first **10** terms of the above series, and also to calculate and print their sum on a different line. The program contains logical and/or syntax errors. Write in your answer booklet six (6) of them, stating **the number of the line** in which each error appears **together with the corrected statement**. (Assume that the statement in line {2} is correct.)

```Pascal
{1}   program askisi7;
{2}   uses wincrt;
{3}   var num,sum:integer;
{4}             cnt:real;
{5}   begin
{6}     num := 0;
{7}     sum := 1;
{8}     for  cnt := 0  to  9  do
{9}       begin
{10}        writeln(num:8);
{11}        sum := sum + 4;
{12}        num := num + 4;
{13}      end;
{14}    writeln;
{15}    writeln(sum:8:2);
{16}  end.
```

