problems.problem:
You are given the following program in the C++ programming language, which uses the input stream **fin** to **read** the marks of **N** students (**1<=N<=1000**) from the file **indata.txt** and store them in the one-dimensional array **vath**. The marks range from **1** to **100** **inclusive**, and a student passes the course if he/she has achieved a mark of **50** points **or more**. Then it uses the output stream **fout** and **prints** at the **end** of the file **outdata.txt** the **marks** of the students who **passed** the course.

```C++
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
using namespace std;
int main(){
     ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │                    Α                     │
     └──────────────────────────────────────────┘
     int i=0,vath[1000],pl;
     ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │                    Β                     │  {
     └──────────────────────────────────────────┘
         fin >> vath[i];
         i++;
     }
     pl=i;
     for(i=0;i<pl;i++)
       if (vath[i]>=50)
         ┌─────────────────────────┐
         │            Γ            │
         └─────────────────────────┘
     fin.close();
     fout.close();
return 0;
}
```

Write in your answer booklet:

(a) The **statements** that must be placed at **position A** so that the appropriate **input** and **output streams** from and to the files are created.

(b) The **statement** that must be placed at **position B** so that the reading of the marks from the file **indata.txt** terminates when all the marks contained in the file have been read.

(c) The **statement** that must be placed at **position Γ** so that the **marks** of the students who **passed** the course are **printed** to the file **outdata.txt**.

